{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BraidsAndKnots.ChiSymAltClosedForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BraidsAndKnots.ChiSymAltClosedForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":35,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProductC_delta_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProductC_delta_zero","kind":"theorem","line":346,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L346-L360","doc":"**The δ = 0 corollary: the colour-blind form is the special case.**\n\nA word whose single colour-weighted letter happens to sit at `d = -H_A/2`\n— i.e. `δ = 0`, the `strict_averaged` convention — has its `pnColour` letter\ncontribute exactly what a `udHalf` letter would, so the product collapses to\nthe colour-blind closed form with the exponent raised by one.\n\nThis is the direction that exists. There is no route back: the colour-blind\nstatement has already discarded `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProductC_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProductC_eq","kind":"theorem","line":316,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L316-L344","doc":"**Closed form on the colour-weighted alphabet.**\n\n    χ_sym(β)·χ_alt(β) = (-1)^{#blind} · (1 + H_A²/4)^{nUd} · Π_{pn} f(d)\n\nThe colour-blind theorem `chiPairProduct_eq` is the case with no `pnColour`\nletters, where `pnProduct = 1` and `#blind = length`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:chi-sym-alt-closed-form","label":"prop:chi-sym-alt-closed-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.pnProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.pnProduct","kind":"def","line":310,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L310-L314","doc":"Product over the colour-weighted letters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.nPn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.nPn","kind":"def","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L304-L308","doc":"Count of colour-weighted letters. One per atom, in the canonical word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.nBlind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.nBlind","kind":"def","line":298,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L298-L302","doc":"Count of colour-blind letters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.nUdC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.nUdC","kind":"def","line":291,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L291-L296","doc":"Count of `udHalf` letters. Matches structurally rather than via `if _ = _`,\nso no `DecidableEq` on the real-carrying type is needed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProductC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProductC","kind":"def","line":287,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L287-L289","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairPerFactorC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairPerFactorC","kind":"def","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L283-L285","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.ColourWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.ColourWord","kind":"def","line":281,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L281-L281","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.ColourFactorType.pnColour","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.ColourFactorType.pnColour","kind":"ctor","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L279-L279","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.ColourFactorType.plain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.ColourFactorType.plain","kind":"ctor","line":278,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L278-L278","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.ColourFactorType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.ColourFactorType","kind":"inductive","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L271-L279","doc":"The alphabet the canonical word uses: the three colour-blind letters, plus\na colour-weighted letter carrying its own `d`.\n\nDeliberately a NEW inductive rather than a fourth constructor on\n`FactorType`: everything above stays exactly as proved, and `FactorType`\nkeeps its `DecidableEq` (which a real-valued field would cost it). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.perFactorOfD_udHalf_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.perFactorOfD_udHalf_le","kind":"theorem","line":264,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L264-L269","doc":"Corollary: the `ud` value is the extremum, and every other letter's value\nlies on one side of it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.four_mul_perFactorOfD_real","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.four_mul_perFactorOfD_real","kind":"theorem","line":259,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L259-L262","doc":"The `ℝ` per-factor product, in the division-free form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.four_mul_perFactorOfD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.four_mul_perFactorOfD","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L234-L257","doc":"**The same content with no division, over any commutative ring.**\n\n    4·(d² − 1 + d·H_A) = (2d + H_A)² − H_A² − 4\n\nThis is the sharper statement, and it is the primary one. Multiplying the\n`ℝ` identity above by 4 clears the `/2`, so it needs no `Field`, no\n`CharZero` and no `2 ≠ 0` — plain `ring` over `[CommRing R]`, which is what\n§7c asks for.\n\nIt also says the thing more directly: **all of the `d`-dependence of the\nper-factor product sits inside a perfect square**, `(2d + H_A)²`, and that\nsquare vanishes exactly at `2d = -H_A`. \"The `ud` letter is a stationary\npoint\" and \"the offset enters squared\" are the same fact, and this form\nmakes the second one manifest without mentioning derivatives, division, or\na distinguished point.\n\nHistorical note worth keeping: the divided form needed `[Field R]\n[CharZero R]`, because `H_A/2` is undefined in characteristic 2 and the\nidentity fails there. This form is fine in characteristic 2 — it degenerates\nto `0 = 0`, which is honest: there is no stationary point to speak of, and\nthe statement makes no claim about one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.perFactorOfD_sub_udHalf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.perFactorOfD_sub_udHalf","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L206-L232","doc":"**The stationarity identity.** For any `d`, the per-factor product differs\nfrom the `ud` value by exactly the SQUARE of the offset:\n\n    perFactorOfD H_A d - perFactorOfD H_A (-H_A/2) = (d + H_A/2)²\n\nThis is the substantive content of this section, and it is a `ring`\nidentity — no calculus needed, and stronger than \"the first derivative\nvanishes\" since it gives the exact remainder.\n\nIt says the `ud` letter sits at a **stationary point** of the per-factor\nproduct, so perturbing it costs SECOND order. That is why the colour\nweighting, a `6.88e-4` relative shift in `d`, moves the character product by\nonly `(7.19e-5)² = 5.17e-9`.\n\nMeasured consequence: `chi_sym_alt_closed_form.py` reported a residual of\n`5.11395e-9` against the colour-blind form on all four atoms; predicted from\nthis identity alone, `5.11397e-9`. Six significant figures. Carrying the p-n\nletter as itself takes the residual to `1.2e-14`, the float64 floor of the\ninputs.\n\nIt is also why the gap stayed hidden: the producer ran in float64 under a\n`tolerance = 1e-3` justified by a comment about \"numerical noise\" in the\nseminormal matrices. There is no such noise, and a real second-order colour\nterm sat 200,000× inside that tolerance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairPerFactor_eq_perFactorOfD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairPerFactor_eq_perFactorOfD","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L200-L204","doc":"`chiPairPerFactor` is `perFactorOfD` at the letter's own `d`. The three\nhard-coded values above are not three separate facts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.dOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.dOf","kind":"def","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L194-L198","doc":"The `d` of each colour-blind letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.perFactorOfD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.perFactorOfD","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L187-L192","doc":"Per-factor character product for the Hecke element `σ + d·1`.\n\nIn the 1-dim irreps `σ ↦ q` (sym) and `σ ↦ -q⁻¹` (alt), so the factor acts\nas `(q + d)` and `(-q⁻¹ + d)`; their product is `d² - 1 + d·H_A`. Every\nletter is an instance of this, including the three of `FactorType`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chi_sym_alt_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chi_sym_alt_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L143-L162","doc":"Existence of a word realizing the closed form.  Combines\n`chi_pair_closed_form` and `n_ud_atom_braid`: some word with\nud-half count `2·(Z+N) + 1` exists and satisfies the closed form.\n\n**Scope note (Copilot PR#401 review).**  As with\n`n_ud_atom_braid`, this is existential only.  Linking it to the\nconcrete `atom_braid_word_3A` output requires formalising that\nPython function in Lean.  The physical content (word length\nparity sign = -1 for all concrete atoms D, T, ³He, ⁴He) is\nverified numerically in\n`computations/derivation_checks.py`; see\ndocs/chi-sym-alt-theorem.md Verification table. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.n_ud_atom_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.n_ud_atom_braid","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L116-L141","doc":"Pure-existence lemma: for every `Z, N ∈ ℕ` there exists a braid\nword whose ud-half count equals `2·(Z+N) + 1`.\n\n**Scope note (Copilot PR#401 review).**  This lemma is *purely\nexistential* and is proven by exhibiting a trivial witness (a list\nof exactly `2·(Z+N) + 1` ud-half factors).  It does **not** prove\nthat the specific word emitted by `atom_braid_word_3A` has this\ncount — that equality is argued informally in\n`docs/chi-sym-alt-theorem.md` § Step 4-5 by inspection of the\nPython source, and is formalization work left for future iteration.\n\nWhen fully formalised, the intended statement becomes:\n  `nUd (atomBraidWord Z N) = 2·(Z+N) + 1`\nwith `atomBraidWord` a Lean port of `mass_at_3A_proper.atom_braid_word_3A`.\n\nRef: [leitner2026] docs/chi-sym-alt-theorem.md § Step 4-5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chi_pair_closed_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chi_pair_closed_form","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L109-L114","doc":"The closed-form theorem in its original stated form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.neg_one_pow_eq_if","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.neg_one_pow_eq_if","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L93-L107","doc":"Auxiliary: (-1 : ℝ)^n equals +1 iff n is even, else -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProduct_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProduct_eq","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L57-L91","doc":"Core lemma: the character product equals (-1)^(length) times the\nud-half scalar raised to its count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.nUd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.nUd","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L52-L55","doc":"Number of ud-half factors in a braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProduct","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairProduct","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L46-L50","doc":"χ_sym(β) · χ_alt(β) computed by multiplicativity over the word.\nDefined via list recursion for clean induction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairPerFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.chiPairPerFactor","kind":"def","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L36-L44","doc":"Per-factor product χ_sym · χ_alt in the two 1-dim Hecke irreps.\n\nFor the Hecke relation σ² = H_A σ + 1 with eigenvalues {q, -q⁻¹},\nχ_sym(σ) = q, χ_alt(σ) = -q⁻¹, and char factors over the word.\nHence χ_sym(cσ+d) · χ_alt(cσ+d) = (cq+d)(-c/q+d) = d² - c² + cd·H_A. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.AtomBraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.AtomBraidWord","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L33-L34","doc":"The atom's braid word is a finite list of (factor-type, generator-index) pairs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.instReprFactorType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.instReprFactorType","kind":"instance","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.instReprFactorType.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.instReprFactorType.repr","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.instDecidableEqFactorType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.instDecidableEqFactorType","kind":"instance","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.FactorType.udHalf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.FactorType.udHalf","kind":"ctor","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L30-L30","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.FactorType.sigmaInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.FactorType.sigmaInv","kind":"ctor","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L29-L29","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.FactorType.sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.FactorType.sigma","kind":"ctor","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L28-L28","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ChiSymAlt.FactorType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ChiSymAlt.FactorType","kind":"inductive","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/braids-and-knots/chi-sym-alt-closed-form.lean#L26-L31","doc":"Factor types arising in atom_braid_word_3A. ","signatureChunk":0}]}